{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"First, we note that $x=-\\dfrac13$ makes the denominator zero and so cannot be a solution.\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3x+1$ to get rid of the quotient. ","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{3x - 2}{3x + 1} \u0026= 3\n\\\\\\\\\n(3x+1)\\cdot \\dfrac{3x - 2}{3x + 1} \u0026= (3x+1)\\cdot 3\n\\\\\\\\\n3x-2\u0026=9x+3\n\\\\\\\\\n-5\u0026=6x\n\\\\\\\\\n-\\dfrac56\u0026=x\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We get that $x=-\\dfrac56$ is a potential solution. It doesn't make the denominator zero, so it is indeed a solution.\n\n**$x = -\\dfrac56$**","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Solve for $x$.**\n\n$\\dfrac{3x - 2}{3x + 1} = 3$\n\n$x =$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"answerForms":["proper","improper"],"maxError":0,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":-0.8333333333333334}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"","multipleNumberInput":false,"size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
